{
 "_doc": "The library clips (issues #529, #539): each move's candidate takes and the `pick` that became assets/animations/library/<move> (judged on the game's men: tools/blender/library_motion.py, tools/library_lineup.gd). Since #539 (Sean on #536's films: the free packs' clips were 'brutal', KayKit a chibi's, the strafe 'highland dancing') the basics are real people from the CMU motion-capture database (B. Hahne's BVH conversion, fetched into build/cmu/ by tools/blender/fetch_library.sh); a take is [source, part, animation, options]: `cycle` [lo, hi] s cuts one loop from a long take's steady middle (find_cycle), `mirror` swaps his sides. `kind`: gait (looped, its phase by the ground he covers), idle (looped by time), once, hold. The aim, the reload and a few others are to come from Uthana (#539 step 3). `drop` (all moves, or a move's own): segments left to the pose: the neck and head (CMU's two neck bones put a kink in ours, the chin poked out). `variant_of`: another walk or run a man may have as his own (LibraryMotion picks one a man by his seed, or config/walks.json's `library` names it). `style`: a variant only a man named to it gets (not in the pool a man's seed picks from). Uthana's takes (#539: the gun moves, $7.50) come from the Studio's motions/gun_moves, copied into build/library_src/uthana/ with its rest pose (motions/card_cheat_rest).",
